CheckS3ForFinalFilesService
  #call
    when S3 has an output file available
      marks the job completed and stores the output URL
      when the job owner is not an APIUser
        does not queue a remediation status notification
    when the job has exceeded the polling time limit
      marks the job failed with a timeout message
      when the job owner is not an APIUser
        does not queue a remediation status notification
    when an error occurs while checking a job
      rescues the error and reports it to Bugsnag
    when the job is missing object_key
      skips checking S3
    when the job is missing filename
      skips checking S3
    when the job record is stale in memory
      reloads the job before checking S3
    when there are many processing jobs
      iterates through all processing jobs
    when the OS sends a termination signal
      stops after the current iteration

S3Handler
  mocked S3 interactions
    #upload_to_input
      uploads a file to S3 input directory
      when an error is raised during the upload
        re-raises an S3Handler::Error
    #presigned_url_for_output
      returns a presigned url if output file exists
      returns nil if output file does not exist
      when an error is raised while retrieving the URL
        re-raises an S3Handler::Error
    #presigned_url_for_input
      returns json with the url, headers, and object_key
      calls the AWS Signer's #presigned_url method

gui_users:import
  when the csv rows have new emails and locations
    creates and links records
  when the gui user exists but the location is new
    updates the user unit association
  when rows are missing required values
    skips invalid rows
  when gui user and unit already exist and are already linked
    does not change persisted data

PageCountQuotaValidator
  .validate!
    when page_count is within quota
      returns true
    when page_count exceeds unit's total quota
      raises QuotaExceededError
    when page_count exceeds user's daily quota
      raises QuotaExceededError
    when owner has no unit
      raises MissingUnitError
    when page_count is not a valid integer
      raises InvalidPageCountError

